  "interpretation": [
    "Shape/contact remains a concrete competing cause: thin current Iron capsules overlap separate imported anatomy pelvis capsule by approximately8.85/8.96cm in unit reference reconstruction. This is not actual RBAN skin collision depth.",
    "New native support resolves previous unknown: each Iron has579 AllPositive vertices and536 Dominant vertices. Current1cm capsule covers0 of both; source broad capsule covers452/579 and418/536. Thus current collider does not fit the supported armor surface; source broad geometry is imported-project evidence, not directly verified original-game metadata.",
    "A thin capsule can lie deep inside the body and generate collision torques while not representing its visible mesh support. These saved facts identify a geometry/contact candidate, but do not prove it causes the published-pose jitter.",
    "Multiplying current savedFrame2 by100 to match the unit relative offset before the engine conversion would apply wrapper compensation twice in the examined RBAN path."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No actual ImmediatePhysics FJointSetup ConnectorTransforms, LastKnownScale, temporary BI.Scale3D, particle actor poses, or first-solve anchor separation were read by this subtask.",
    "The unit-ref reconstructed anchor gap is conditional on examined engine path/default body scale and is not a measured animated pre-sim or live contact-frame gap. Ref-pose temporary actor creation positions retain the imported wrapper; RBAN subsequently resets bodies from output pose before normal simulation.",
    "Body anatomy and Leg imported reference skeleton poses differ; ref collider overlap and reference skin support are not proof of animated skinned-body clearance.",
    "BaselineIronPhysicsAudit.frame1/frame2 are default stored frames only; quaternion/position serialized6decimal digits bounds precision. Existing raw helper records do not export actual effective joint translations.",
    "Collision point-plane cached separation can be stale; InitialPhi/current contact metrics cannot assert zero visible skin penetration.",
